0031:     """
0032:     Swap the two colored fills inside the unique rectangular frame while preserving black gaps.
0033: 
0034:     Input structure:
0035:     - The grid contains one one-cell-thick rectangular frame.
0036:     - The frame interior contains black pixels and exactly two non-black, non-frame colors.
0037:     - Pixels outside the frame may use the same colors but are not part of the editable region.
0038: 
0039:     Rule:
0040:     - Find the unique rectangular frame and take the region strictly inside it.
0041:     - Within that interior, exchange the two non-black, non-frame colors.
0042:     - Preserve black interior pixels, the frame, and all pixels outside the frame.
0043: 
0044:     Key insight:
0045:     - The frame, not the outer scattered pixels, selects the only region where the color swap applies.
